meta { name: Dashboard summary, type: http, seq: 1 }

get { url: {{adminBase}}/dashboard, body: none, auth: none }

headers { Cookie: {{sessionCookie}} }

docs {
  The first screen after login. One endpoint, two shapes, chosen server-side
  from the resolved principal — the caller cannot ask for the other one.

  As a tenant author:
    tenant-wide article counts, this author's own counts, media count, and the
    8 most recently EDITED articles (any status, ordered by updated_at).

  As a platform admin:
    every tenant with authorCount / publishedCount / draftCount, and nothing
    else. AGGREGATES ONLY — no article titles, slugs, or content. Root
    CLAUDE.md §1 gives a platform admin no access to any tenant's content, and a
    title appearing here would be a reversal of that, not a new field.

  Worth re-checking after any change to the tenant stats query: it once returned
  zero for every count (a correlated subquery that did not correlate), which
  looks exactly like a brand-new installation rather than an error. There are
  now repository tests asserting the counts are non-zero.

  Full shapes in core-engine/docs/api-reference.md.
}
